===BODY===
          <h2>On the Autoroute du Soleil</h2>
          <p>The A6 from Paris and the A7 to the Mediterranean, together the &ldquo;Autoroute du Soleil&rdquo;, pass right through Lyon, including the Fourvière tunnel, a notorious bottleneck in summer. Long queues in hot weather mean plenty of overheating and breakdowns, especially for heavily loaded holiday cars and caravans.</p>

          <h2>Off the motorway first</h2>
          <p>On French motorways, the official breakdown operator for that stretch tows you off the motorway to their garage, at a regulated price. Use the orange emergency phones or call 112. Once the car is at the garage, send us the address and we'll bring it home.</p>

          <h2>Where we collect from</h2>
          <p>We collect from Lyon and the surrounding area, the Rhône valley down towards Valence, and towards the Alps (Grenoble, Annecy, Chambéry). Lyon has a low emission zone (ZFE) that needs a Crit&rsquo;Air sticker to drive in, including for UK cars, but that doesn't affect a collection by transporter.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Towing a caravan?</strong> Tell us when you ask for a quote. A car and a caravan may need to be moved separately, and we'll plan for that.</p>
          </div>
===FAQ===
Q: How long does it take to bring a car back from Lyon?
A: It's a long way to the Channel, around 750 km. We'll give you an expected collection and delivery time with the quote.
Q: Can you bring back a car and a caravan?
A: Often, yes, but they may travel separately. Tell us the size of the caravan when you ask for a quote.
Q: Can you talk to the French garage for me?
A: Yes. We speak French and can arrange collection directly with the garage.
